# Data Handling Rules

## Design Mode Constraints

This is a **prototype in Design Mode**. Keep data handling simple and frontend-only.

### What This Means

- **Static data only**: All data comes from static TypeScript files
- **No APIs**: No backend API calls
- **No databases**: No database connections
- **No mocking**: Don't mock APIs or databases - use real static data

## Data Files

### Location

Store data files in `src/lib/data/`:

```
src/lib/data/
├── journeys-registry.ts  # Journey registry (imports from journey folders)
└── sprints.ts            # Sprint data (optional)
```

### Type Definitions

Store types in `src/lib/types/`:

```
src/lib/types/
└── journey.ts            # Journey type definitions
```

## Journey Data Structure

### Types (`src/lib/types/journey.ts`)

```typescript
export interface JourneyPage {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  path: string;
  description?: string;
}

export interface JourneyConfig {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  status: 'in-progress' | 'draft' | 'completed';
  pages: JourneyPage[];
}
```

### Journey Metadata Files

Each journey folder contains its own `_journey.ts`:

```typescript
// src/app/prototype/journeys/onboarding/_journey.ts
import type { JourneyConfig } from '@/lib/types/journey';

export const journey: JourneyConfig = {
  id: 'onboarding',
  title: 'Onboarding Flow',
  description: 'New user registration and setup',
  status: 'in-progress',
  pages: [
    { id: 'login', name: 'Login', path: '/prototype/journeys/onboarding/login' },
    { id: 'signup', name: 'Sign Up', path: '/prototype/journeys/onboarding/signup' },
  ],
};
```

### Journey Registry

Central registry imports all journeys:

```typescript
// src/lib/data/journeys-registry.ts
import type { JourneyConfig } from '@/lib/types/journey';
import { journey as banking } from '@/app/prototype/journeys/banking/_journey';
import { journey as checkoutFlow } from '@/app/prototype/journeys/checkout-flow/_journey';

export const journeys: JourneyConfig[] = [
  banking,
  checkoutFlow,
];

export function getJourney(id: string): JourneyConfig | undefined {
  return journeys.find(j => j.id === id);
}

export function getAllJourneys(): JourneyConfig[] {
  return journeys;
}

export function getAllJourneyIds(): string[] {
  return journeys.map(j => j.id);
}

export function getJourneysByStatus(status: JourneyConfig['status']): JourneyConfig[] {
  return journeys.filter(j => j.status === status);
}
```

## Usage in Components

```tsx
// Import from registry
import { getAllJourneys, getJourney } from "@/lib/data/journeys-registry";

function JourneyList() {
  const journeys = getAllJourneys();
  
  return (
    <div>
      {journeys.map((journey) => (
        <div key={journey.id}>{journey.title}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Type Safety

- Always use TypeScript interfaces
- Import types from `@/lib/types/journey`
- Use helper functions from registry

## Static Data Files (Non-Journey)

For other static data (products, users, etc.):

### Location
- `src/lib/data/` for TypeScript data files
- `public/data/` for JSON files needing public access

### Structure

```typescript
// src/lib/data/products.ts
export interface Product {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  category: string;
  price: number;
}

export const products: Product[] = [
  { id: '1', name: 'Product Name', category: 'Electronics', price: 99.99 },
];

export function getProduct(id: string): Product | undefined {
  return products.find(p => p.id === id);
}

export function getAllProducts(): Product[] {
  return products;
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Type everything** - All data must have TypeScript interfaces
2. **Use helper functions** - Don't access data directly
3. **Keep schemas simple** - Prototype-focused, not production database
4. **Direct imports** - Reference data files directly
5. **Descriptive IDs** - Use meaningful kebab-case IDs
6. **One source of truth** - Don't duplicate data

## What NOT to Do

- Don't create mock API functions
- Don't simulate network delays
- Don't build fake backend patterns
- Don't over-engineer data structures
- Don't create complex data relationships
- Don't duplicate data in multiple places
- Don't hardcode data in components
